            <history xml:id="history_254N2015C">
               <p xml:id="idm110">This Concert Overture differs from the other overtures by Hartmann - apart from the two juvenile overtures (HartW 30) and (HartW 31) - by not having a programme. As the overture had its first performance in the spring of 1853, when the permanent conductor of Musikforeningen, Niels W. Gade, led the Gewandhaus concerts in Leipzig, Hartmann himself conducted this concert.</p>
